# nsmbudx.sym -- NSMBU Deluxe (Switch) symbol addresses
#
# Format: `name = 0xADDRESS;` where ADDRESS is an in-image address (VA - 0x60000000).
#
# IMPORTANT: do not list a symbol here if our own subsdk code defines it.
#
# IMPORTANT: NEVER list crt0.s / runtime labels here. sweet-dx turns each entry into an
# ABSOLUTE linker-script assignment, which overrides crt0's own definition. Listing
# `_init = 0x24;` made the linker script clobber crt0's `_init`, and because 0x24 is
# below 0xCD1000 it wrapped to 0xFF32F024, so the emitted module shipped
# DT_INIT = 0xFF32F024 -- an entry point outside the module. The dynamic loader branched
# there at startup, resource loading half-failed, and models rendered as black figures
# while the game kept running. That was the whole "rendering bug".
#
# Forbidden names (crt0.s / linker.ld provide them; never redefine them here):
#   _init  _fini  _start  _crt0_section  static_init_hook
#   __mod0_start  __bss_start__  __bss_end__
#   __eh_frame_hdr_start  __eh_frame_hdr_end
#
# Verify every build with:
#   python .rea/verify_subsdk0.py <output>/.../exefs/subsdk0
# It must report DT_INIT inside .text (it should be 0x24). See
# sweetdx/docs/SUBSDK0_DT_INIT_ROOT_CAUSE.md.
#
# sweet-dx converts every entry into an absolute linker-script assignment of
# `address - NSMBUDX_NSO_MEMORY_SIZE` (0xCD1000). For addresses below that offset the
# value wraps negative into 0xFFxxxxxx, and any hook on it then tries to branch to
# 0x100xxxxxx -- outside the +-32 MiB ARM branch range. We hit exactly that:
#
#     Branch from 0x000182A0 to 0x1000182A0 is out of range
#
# caused by listing Profile::get (0x182A0) and the Profile constructor (0x17F6C) here
# while profile.cpp compiles its own versions into subsdk0. Those two are removed; the
# addresses are preserved in symbols/nsmbudx_removed.sym for reference.

# nsmbudx.sym -- symbols for New Super Mario Bros. U Deluxe v1.0.0
# Generated from the nsmbud-reverse IDB inventory.
#
# SweetDX format: 'name = 0xADDRESS;'  ('#' starts a comment)
# Addresses are in-image addresses (VA - 0x60000000) and are
# strictly below NSMBUDX_NSO_MEMORY_SIZE (0x00CD1000).
#
# symbols: 3174
#
# Name corrections applied (verified against disassembly):
#   _ZN10StageActor18directionToPlayerXERK4Vec2
#     -> _ZN10StageActor18directionToPlayerHERK4Vec3
#   _ZN10StageActor18directionToPlayerYERK4Vec2
#     -> _ZN10StageActor18directionToPlayerVERK4Vec3
#   _ZN10StageActor9befreDrawEv
#     -> _ZN10StageActor10beforeDrawEv
#   _ZN5Enemy4vfD0Ev
#     -> _ZN5Enemy6freezeEv

